            <ArticleTitle>Sickle cell hepatopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sickle cell hepatopathy is a well-documented entity that ranges from the self-limiting hepatic right upper quadrant syndrome to the potentially lethal intrahepatic cholestasis and acute hepatic sequestration syndromes. We describe a 26-year-male with homozygous sickle cell disease who had this unique hepatic presentation and was documented to have characteristic findings of cholestasis, portal inflammation and sinusoidal dilatation on histopathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
